      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not define what RAVLT is (e.g., that it is a “cognitive assessment measure”); it only reports “explicit memory (RAVLT delayed recall)” and gives delayed recall scores.",
        "The claim that RAVLT is “particularly” for delayed recall is not explicitly stated; the packet only specifies that the outcome used was “RAVLT delayed recall.”",
        "The statement about directionality (“higher RAVLT delayed recall scores indicated better postoperative memory performance”) is supported for this study (higher scores in the dexmedetomidine group), but the overall definition includes additional unsupported characterization of the measure."
